  $t$The operational document holds the rule: version 146, written by W3 at 18:05 CST 2026-11-24 on the operator's press "Write it", one paragraph of 466 characters added in section 30 after THE REVIEW AFTER A RUN and before DENIALS, TIMEOUTS AND WRITES, nothing deleted (audit 41802; operational_doc_log row 110). W1 read it back MATCH (Wall 11814): v146 less the paragraph and one blank line equals v145; the paragraph equals the graded draft's. The plan's DONE is at the readback. Criterion (d), the next AAR sent carries the cost under the rule: the AAR of run 42373, draft 6 (aar/w3/aar_run42373_draft6.md 6ef38f57; W1 PASS, Wall 11875) states the stored cost 10.12 in its RUN part, names the question-round calls that had no cost entry, and gives the true cost about 11.45 from W4's count; it is drafted and graded, NOT YET SENT to the operator at the time of this draft. No engine, child, database function, Wall manual or corpus text changed. Related, not part of this ASK: ASK 627 (written 18:20 CST, audit 41819) repairs the list of priced calls, so later runs store the whole cost.$t$,
